# One entry per line, 10 fields separated by '|':
#   id|group|folder|kind|source|pattern|checksum|persist|extract|trust
# group:    core | windows | android | tool   (windows/android follow ventoy-usb.conf)
# folder:   path on the drive; '@tools' is cached under .tools/ and never copied to the drive
# kind:     dirsums | github | dirindex | sfrss | archive | latesturl | windows | manual
#           Every kind resolves the newest upstream version at run time; nothing is pinned.
# pattern:  ERE that names the entry's files; older files matching it are replaced automatically
# checksum: sums:<file> | gh-digest | sidecar:<suffix> | rss-hash | archive-hash | none:<reason>
#           A missing checksum fails that entry. Only none:<reason> skips verification.
# persist:  Ventoy persistence label; the entry gets a ventoy.json persistence block.
# extract:  ERE of the archive member to extract after download (needs 7z).
# trust:    gpg:<fingerprint>:<signature suffix>:<key url> | two-origin | same-origin-digest | none
#           gpg verifies the checksum file against the vendor key; two-origin checks a second site;
#           same-origin-digest only detects corruption; none follows an explicit none:<reason>.
